# SOP always-on

This workspace has **one** auto-entry: skill `sop-orchestrator`.

On every user message:

1. Identify intent → STAGE / role (`routing.md`).
2. If 修改 / 门禁 / 目标 / 改代码 / 失败 → 分诊 first (`impact.md`). Direct CODE edits still need upstream check.
3. Resolve user/path/CURRENT/state slugs; warn and stop writes on mismatch.
4. Print the role banner, then select **one primary STAGE suite**. Read its
   entry/root `SKILL.md`; only that suite may explicitly activate internal
   workers, one at a time, under its own budget. Never ambient-load workers or
   another STAGE.
5. Write stage artifacts in sibling roots (`workspace-map.md`), not into this
   repo except orchestration state / `intake/` / `test/` / `docs/`.
6. After any runtime-affecting CODE change: TEST `mode=regression` via
   `project-test` scripts; read `last-run.json`.
7. Gates use stable IDs from `governance.md`: show evidence in chat, obtain
   explicit user confirmation, then record APPROVALS/DECISIONS/SOP. Machine
   evidence/state never approves; never parse Markdown checkboxes.
8. Tools: `tools.md`. Browser = `cursor-ide-browser`. Product tests = MCP
   `playwright` + regression scripts. UI workers run serially
   (`prd-pack-ingest` → `visual-choice-first` → `frontend-design-studio`).
   ARCH peers = `.cursor/skills/peers/`, phase allowlists only (normally ≤2;
   the grill pair counts as 2). CODE/PPT keep their existing budgets.
9. Historical/existing project → INTAKE first: complete ledger, evidence, gaps,
   and stage handoffs before iteration.
10. PPT is explicit-intent only. Existing `.ppt/.pptx`, slide references, or
   historical slide extraction never load `ppt-deck`.
11. Delivery ends at DOCS. RELEASE/OPS/maintenance stages and roles are
    deferred.

Do not auto-load transplanted or peer skills. They have `disable-model-invocation: true`.
